In the video, 50 seems pretty annoyed that he has to throw out his favorite snacks and essentially gives his followers a public service announcement in the form of a reminder to get rid of them if you have one of the five flavors that had been recalled.

&#8220;OK, now, if you eat these, they got a recall because there might be f&#8212;in&#8217; glass in them, so you gotta throw them out,&#8221; he said begrudgingly. &#8220;Can&#8217;t even eat pops no more. What the f&#8212;?&#8221; He then doubled down in a caption that read, &#8220;Can’t eat lettuce can’t eat popsicles they recalled 5 flavors because glass may be in them. Just throw the sh&#8211; out !&#8221;

View this post on Instagram

Watermelon, grape, tangerine, black cherry and strawberry are the five flavors that have been recalled.

The FDA posted a statement from Dreyer&#8217;s along with batch codes and best before dates. You can read the statement here: &#8220;Dreyer’s Grand Ice Cream, Inc. is voluntarily recalling a limited number of select flavors of Outshine Fruit Bars due to possible foreign material contamination with glass. Products affected include Outshine Strawberry, Watermelon, Grape, Tangerine and Black Cherry 6-Count 2.5 ounce Fruit Bars and the Outshine 24-Count 2.5 ounce Variety Pack Fruit Bars.&#8221;

As long as the pomegranate flavor isn&#8217;t on the list, then we should be good.
